## Hints

- `dict[price] -> collections.deque[[order_id, qty]]` per side gives you FIFO
  for free; a second dict `order_id -> (side, price)` makes cancel O(level).
- `max(bids)` / `min(asks)` are fine here — a real matching engine would keep
  sorted levels (see the lesson's discussion of why), but correctness first.
- The FIFO-at-same-price tests are the heart of this exercise: queue position
  is half of why latency matters in HFT.

